    "setupNotes": [
      "Factorio 2.1.24 Space Age. 19 assembling machine 2 (no modules), red belts, fast/long-handed/bulk arms. WEST inputs, one labelled entrance each: iron plates, electronic circuits, copper plates, steel plates, stone bricks, plastic bars. EAST: eight passive provider chests in one column, one product each; each stops at its own cap, set in the constant combinator beside the fast-belt chest (edit one number). Gears, cable, red circuits, yellow belts, undergrounds, splitters, inserters and AM1 are made inside. Preserve the red ring wires, the green cap wires, all arm filters, the gear clock and the fast-inserter reserve decider. Supply electricity at the marked substation.",
      "Feed each west entrance with its labelled material only; the harness feeds every entrance as a full red belt. Iron mostly goes to the rear belt behind the bottom row (gear machines, AM1, yellow splitters, fast inserters); the ring takes its share through one admission arm.",
      "Electronic circuits are a supplied input (84/min at the floors, more when one product is drawn alone); one green-circuits supplier covers this mall.",
      "Caps live in one constant combinator next to the fast-belt chest (one negative number per product). Each chest arm runs only while its product is below its cap.",
      "Fast inserters are also a bulk-inserter ingredient: their feed arm stops while the fast-inserter chest is full, and a decider keeps a reserve of fast inserters on the ring for the bulk-inserter machine.",
      "Gear arms of the six gear-hungry finals take turns in an eight-window clock (7.5 s each); yellow belts, inserters and AM1 take gears freely because their own ring limits bound them."
